  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>%</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>56</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>As per the colour code for carbon resistors, the colour assigned to numbers</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> Green<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> Blue<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> Orange</p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>%</mo></math> accuracy or tolerance, the colour is silver. Hence, the bands of colours of carbon resistor in sequence are green, blue, orange and silver.</p>"
